The three faces the Classical design system is set in.

    Cormorant Garamond   headings, display figures, stat values
    Lora                 body text, stat labels, the subhead
    Courier Prime        the sigil, kickers, numerals, history, footer

All three are SIL Open Font Licence 1.1, which is what makes shipping them
possible; each licence is beside its font as OFL-<name>.txt.  They came from
github.com/google/fonts.  Cormorant Garamond and Lora are variable fonts, so
one file carries every weight; Courier Prime is three statics.

They are not installed.  main-tcl.c's fonts_register() hands them to the
platform at startup in *process* scope, so they exist for as long as the game
runs and leave nothing behind -- Tk has no API for loading a font file, it asks
the platform for a family by name and takes what it is given, so the platform
has to be told first.  On macOS that is CTFontManagerRegisterFontsForURL.
Windows wants AddFontResourceEx and Linux FcConfigAppFontAddFile; neither is
written yet, and until they are, those builds fall back to the chain named in
lib/tcl/classical.tcl.

The .fon files here are something else entirely: bitmap fonts for the Windows
terminal build, and nothing to do with the above.
